  "text": "Imagine end-to-end tests you never write. Or remember to run. Introducing Replay Q A. Point it at your app. No test suite needed. Just a quick chat. It explores your app in a real browser. Turns what it finds into user journeys, and runs them. Then it runs on Replay's browsers. On a schedule, while you sleep. Against staging, a preview, even local host. And on every pull request. Each run is recorded, then reviewed. For what breaks, and what's slow. Some bugs only exist in time. Replay Q A caught one in its own app. One update. Sixty-seven milliseconds. Four dropped frames.",
